// Regression fixture pinning the Task 7 review-fix behavior (memory-
// audit-4e whole-branch review, probe P4): a LOCAL container's element read
// escapes to a global. `p4Items[0]` is a list-INDEX read (`EIndexRef` at
// the IR level -- a raw `rt_list_at` borrow, never itself retained by
// cprint, unlike a MAP subscript's `IMapGet` intrinsic, which does retain
// internally -- see `lowStoreIntrOwnsResult`'s own doc comment for that
// distinction) -- reading it disqualifies `p4Items` from a DEEP scope-exit
// release (the escape walker's `lowEscapeContainerElemRisky` rule: an
// element handle the container itself still owns can escape through an
// index read), same rule/reasoning as before ARC Task 4, untouched by it
// (container elements are Task 5's still-unmigrated slot class).
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores): `p4GSaved = p4Items[0]` is a
// NAMED-SLOT store (global) whose source is a non-birth element read --
// `lowCountedStore` retains it FIRST (confirmed against the emitted C:
// `rt_text_retain(cv___store1)` immediately after the `rt_list_at` borrow),
// THEN releases `p4GSaved`'s OLD (default-empty) handle -- a real free now,
// not the permanent orphan-on-overwrite this comment used to describe.
// `p4Items` itself (the container's OWN handle, disqualified from DEEP
// release only) still gets a real, unconditional SHALLOW release at scope
// exit (`rt_list_release(cv_p4Items)`, confirmed against the emitted C --
// Task 4's own "unconditional local release" applying to `p4Items`'s own
// box, not its elements) -- so the list's struct box + backing array are no
// longer leaked either. Expected strict-mode leak count: 2 (see
// ../p4_elem_escape.leaks, dropped from 6) -- only the shared `"a"+"b"`
// text handle itself (2 blocks): `p4Items`'s shallow release disposes the
// container without walking into it (deep release stays gated on the SAME
// proof 4e always required -- Task 5's still-unmigrated container-element
// class), and `p4GSaved`, a global, is never itself released
// (`cl_free_globals` stays empty -- Task 6's still-unmigrated slot class).
// Not a bug -- both are explicitly out of this task's scope.

var p4GSaved: text

func runP4ElemEscape() {
    var p4Items: list of text
    p4Items.push("a" + "b")
    p4GSaved = p4Items[0]
    alert("p4 done")
}
